<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Avalanche in Nepal leaves 2 dead, several missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59201c5ec651925471cb7f4e5658a2d5038c70b9850507c37e866f308fca56b7</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T17:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101--fcbca2d1e804.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/avalanche-in-nepal-leaves-2-dead-several-missing/a-79450101?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An avalanche has struck the Himlung Himal base camp in Nepal after days of severe weather. Two guides are confirmed dead and at least 14 people remain missing in the remote region.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Kolkata's SRFTI students allege violent attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0fb8c17ba4611ce984e178ff017797554495e38296dbc2b007383bb8fa54545</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T08:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869--92d965222a7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-kolkata-s-srfti-students-allege-violent-attack/live-79440869?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students at Kolkata's Satyajit Ray Film and Television Institute say they were attacked with knives after confronting an outside group over a meeting they allege was affiliated with the right-wing Hindu RSS.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China sends two giant pandas off to Atlanta zoo after Xi-Trump summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:974b02fc68b169a6e47d16dc0bfc2ac18235530e5467c22590cce750c9dcf03a</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-27T07:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128--ab8e1682ffd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-sends-two-giant-pandas-off-to-atlanta-zoo-after-xi-trump-summit/a-79447128?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ping Ping and Fu Shuang took off to Atlanta on a FedEx plane, with steamed corn buns, carrots and bamboo to snack on during the flight. Their trip is one of the few concrete things to come out the Xi-Trump summit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China, US agree to set up channel for AI safety incidents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:49075879b425af08c94e6a95f966bc9043efa0759aca35b6ea87e9e44fb41261</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T16:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351--116e0ce66bfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-us-agree-to-set-up-channel-for-ai-safety-incidents/a-79443351?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following the summit between US President Donald Trump and Chinese President Xi Jinping, the two superpowers pledged to set up a "communication channel" for AI incidents and boost coordination on military matters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Suicide attack at police stop kills at least 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df18f032855ab27d64c4cd203e5578aeaece8d019535fddf0e9ff696adf9087f</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050--24fa32f41a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-suicide-attack-at-police-stop-kills-at-least-11/a-79443050?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The blast was claimed by the Pakistani Taliban, which has stepped up attacks on Pakistani security forces in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea's gender pay gap grows as women get older</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34f87e0513bb8c948aa6e73881276f010d4ad7d2ef1e4ff3fce95fdc467df1d9</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T10:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285--9ddac1458d8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-s-gender-pay-gap-grows-as-women-get-older/a-79431285?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new report shows how in South Korea, women on average earn less and have fewer employment opportunities throughout their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Thailand: Bangkok flooding triggers disaster declaration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:009abef91e0531678a33eaa3347a5322921cdc28b9b595b0c913223281cbacf0</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-26T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575--24f35b64d6d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thailand-bangkok-flooding-triggers-disaster-declaration/a-79440575?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rainfall over the past three days has caused heavy flooding in the Thai capital. A state of disaster has been declared in all 50 districts in Bangkok.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>After Xi-Trump summit, US-China rivalry remains frozen. Is this to Beijing's advantage?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5064c641ea3faf02b5f9b4107e806ec206a73768167fabc8f9c9ed753cc555e5</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T11:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127--110c4fa9d052.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-xi-trump-summit-us-china-rivalry-remains-frozen-is-this-to-beijing-s-advantage/a-79427127?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president showcased White House construction projects and hosted a lavish dinner with tech CEOs, but the summit made little progress on key issues such as trade tensions and AI regulation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan: Khan family arrests raise stakes ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc8462ab4856a8487847b28c8c7ce80256762ba997c4825369fef2df46d1a977</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T13:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147--cb3db8a0de02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-khan-family-arrests-raise-stakes-ahead-of-protests/a-79392147?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sons of Pakistan's jailed former Prime Minister Imran Khan told DW their father is in ill health while being isolated from family and doctors. Other relatives have been detained ahead of a planned opposition protest.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal rejects 'sympathy,' asks for $20 million after floods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f6982eb2bffaf4ac57472156c879fb8afee172993ba510214deca7333d1b183</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-mill-after-floods/a-79372239--b0482f9bc73a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-rejects-sympathy-asks-for-20-million-after-floods/a-79372239?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With Nepal still reeling from the devastating floods in August, Kathmandu is calling for climate justice and seeking compensation from the UN-backed Loss and Damage Fund, Environment Minister Geeta Chaudhary told DW.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Could we see MMA at the Olympics?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d1b68e9624d96fc87bb1e1bab2e370c9709a450a134f1bbead5c5a298054bd4</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T12:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605--f76e8af14c92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/could-we-see-mma-at-the-olympics/a-79369605?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mixed martial arts has made its debut at the Asian Games this week. It takes the sport closer to the Olympics, but there are doubts about the next step — and the influence of the popular and lucrative UFC.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Male infertility is 'grossly underreported'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c51e146751b26d206c50a6267770546903a7e5d2d6d5071afd12be82a716639</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722--14a06576edd4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/male-infertility-is-grossly-underreported/a-79368722?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">It's not all on women anymore — doctors do test men for sperm count and motility. But still too few men get checked, possibly due to a misconception that a healthy sex life means healthy sperm. Spoiler: It doesn't.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>As Trump-Xi summit nears, Europe is caught in middle of US-China rivalry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45939eb17182fd7b234e2e15a738489b03ddebb70d30484a29a62e9627e6afe2</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540--3c6355b77845.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-trump-xi-summit-nears-europe-is-caught-in-middle-of-us-china-rivalry/a-79356540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China's Xi Jinping is traveling to Washington this week. Regardless of what comes from his talks with US President Trump, the EU will likely remain stuck between erratic US trade policy and Beijing's export machine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nuclear power is back on Southeast Asia's energy agenda</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e435a2c9c8038121bc3354d5bc1691d09cd538a7e2ed7a695bad0711ff5fae63</id><updated>2026-09-27T19:49:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-21T13:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744--70fdccf67ff5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nuclear-power-is-back-on-southeast-asia-s-energy-agenda/a-79358744?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising electricity demand, shocks in energy security and climate commitments are reviving long-stalled plans for nuclear power across Southeast Asia. But proponents of nuclear energy still face major obstacles.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
